    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **50 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic and folded the household into the duplicate-detection logic, per the specification.\n\n### Changes to `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`\n\n1. **`householdId` is now always computed and deterministic.** Previously it was only derived (from last name + address) when `sharesHousehold` was set, and was `null` otherwise. Now it is the first 12 hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`, computed for every owner regardless of `sharesHousehold`. Owners sharing a last name and postcode automatically derive the same id.\n\n2. **`sharesHousehold` now only bypasses the duplicate block.** Because the household is keyed on (last name, postcode), any existing owner carrying the computed `householdId` is already a member of that household. A second such owner is rejected as a household duplicate (`409` via `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException`) unless it sets `sharesHousehold`, in which case it is admitted as a declared member.\n\n3. **Removed the backfill loop.** No longer needed \u2014 every member independently derives the same stable id at creation time.\n\n4. **Declared members are not flagged as suspected duplicates.** Soft-match detection is skipped when `sharesHousehold` is set; any non-declared owner reaching that point shares no household (a household match without `sharesHousehold` was already rejected).\n\nDuplicate detection (the consolidated identity key) and the household-size input to the membership level already key off `householdId`, so both now use the computed value. The identity-key check still fires first, so a full duplicate (same telephone/email/household) is rejected `409` even with `sharesHousehold` set (Cp28).\n\n### Documentation\nUpdated the `sharesHousehold` and `householdId` descriptions in `openapi.yml` to reflect the new (last name, postcode) keying and deterministic derivation.",
